<main class="container">

  <div class="hero">
    <div class="eyebrow">Product Case Study · Lending Technology</div>
    <h1>Making lending products configurable, scalable and easier to manage.</h1>
    <p class="subtitle muted">
      Building configurable lending infrastructure that enables
      businesses and financial partners to define loan products,
      commercial rules, credit assessment criteria, and approval
      workflows through a reusable platform.
    </p>

    <div class="meta">
      <div class="panel">
        <strong>My Role</strong>
        Lead Product Manager
      </div>
      <div class="panel">
        <strong>Ownership</strong>
        Product Vision & End-to-End Scope
      </div>
      <div class="panel">
        <strong>Delivery</strong>
        MVP Shipped
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>

  <section>
    <div class="eyebrow">01 · The Challenge</div>
    <h2>Different lending products shouldn't require rebuilding the same capabilities.</h2>
    <p class="muted">
      Lending businesses and financial partners have different
      commercial models, customer segments, risk appetites,
      and approval requirements.
    </p>
    <p class="muted">
      Configuring and managing these variations can become
      operationally complex when product rules and workflows
      are not sufficiently flexible.
    </p>
    <p class="muted">
      The opportunity was to create a configurable lending
      capability that could support different loan products
      and operational requirements without treating every
      new product or partner as an entirely separate build.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <div class="eyebrow">02 · Product Vision</div>
    <h2>Move from rigid lending processes to configurable capabilities.</h2>
    <p class="muted">
      I led the product vision, strategy, and end-to-end scope
      for an automation capability designed to make loan
      product configuration and lending workflows more
      flexible.
    </p>

    <div class="highlight">
      The central product idea was to make key lending rules
      configurable, allowing the business to support different
      products and partner requirements through a reusable
      lending service.
    </div>

    <div class="grid">
      <div class="panel">
        <h3>Configurable Loan Products</h3>
        <p>
          Define and configure different loan products
          according to business and partner requirements.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="panel">
        <h3>Commercial Fee Configuration</h3>
        <p>
          Configure commercial fees and product-specific
          lending parameters.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="panel">
        <h3>Credit Assessment</h3>
        <p>
          Configure credit assessment criteria to support
          different lending propositions.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="panel">
        <h3>Approval Workflows</h3>
        <p>
          Configure review and approval workflows to support
          lending decision processes.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <div class="eyebrow">03 · Product Experience</div>
    <h2>How the capability works.</h2>
    <p class="muted">
      The MVP brought several important lending configuration
      capabilities into a more structured product experience.
    </p>

    <div class="step">
      <strong>01. Define the loan product</strong>
      <p class="muted">
        Set up the loan product and its core parameters
        according to the intended lending proposition.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="step">
      <strong>02. Configure commercial terms</strong>
      <p class="muted">
        Define applicable commercial fees and other
        product-specific rules.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="step">
      <strong>03. Define credit assessment requirements</strong>
      <p class="muted">
        Configure the assessment criteria used to evaluate
        applications under the product.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="step">
      <strong>04. Configure approval workflows</strong>
      <p class="muted">
        Establish the review and approval process that
        applications must follow.
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="step">
      <strong>05. Support lending operations</strong>
      <p class="muted">
        Make the configured lending proposition available
        for operational use within the supported service.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <div class="eyebrow">04 · My Role & Contribution</div>
    <h2>Leading product definition and cross-functional delivery.</h2>
    <p class="muted">
      I owned the product vision and scope, connecting
      business needs with the requirements needed to
      deliver the MVP.
    </p>
    <ul>
      <li>Defined the product vision, strategy, scope, and priorities.</li>
      <li>Created product requirements documents (PRDs) and technical requirements documents (TRDs).</li>
      <li>Developed risk matrices to identify and communicate product and delivery risks.</li>
      <li>Created sequence diagrams to clarify system interactions and workflows.</li>
      <li>Defined partner API contracts and data consent requirements.</li>
      <li>Conducted market research and contributed to product positioning.</li>
      <li>Supported go-to-market planning and stakeholder workshops.</li>
      <li>Coordinated cross-functional stakeholders through product definition and MVP delivery.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section>
    <div class="eyebrow">05 · Delivery & Adoption</div>
    <h2>From an internal capability to a reusable lending service.</h2>
    <p class="muted">
      The MVP was shipped with capabilities for configuring
      loan products, commercial fees, credit assessment,
      and approval workflows.
    </p>
    <p class="muted">
      Beyond supporting VendorCredit's lending operations,
      the capability was designed to support financial
      partners seeking a white-label lending service.
    </p>

    <div class="highlight">
      The strategic value was not simply automating individual
      tasks. It was creating a configurable foundation that
      could support multiple lending propositions and partner
      requirements.
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <div class="eyebrow">06 · Business Impact</div>
    <h2>Creating a foundation for operational flexibility and scale.</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Shipped an MVP covering core loan product configuration capabilities.</li>
      <li>Established configurable commercial fee, credit assessment, and approval workflow capabilities.</li>
      <li>Created a reusable lending service proposition for internal and potential white-label partner use.</li>
      <li>Provided a foundation for supporting different lending products and partner requirements.</li>
    </ul>
    <p class="muted">
      Quantitative improvements in processing time, operational
      efficiency, and credit performance are not included here
      because verified figures have not yet been established.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <div class="eyebrow">07 · What This Demonstrates</div>
    <h2>Thinking in reusable product capabilities, not one-off solutions.</h2>
    <p class="muted">
      This initiative demonstrates my ability to identify
      repeatable business needs and translate them into
      configurable product capabilities.
    </p>
    <p class="muted">
      It also highlights my experience working across product
      strategy, lending operations, technical requirements,
      risk considerations, partner needs, and cross-functional
      delivery.
    </p>
  </section>

